char inputBuffer[14]; fgets(inputBuffer, 14, stdin)`.\n\nB. `print_cstr` uses `libc::printf(\"%s\\n\", ptr)`. Compare against C's `printf(\"%s\\n\", line)`\n   for very long strings (e.g. 100 KB), strings with `%` sequences, and non-UTF-8 bytes.\n   Also check `printIntLine` via `printf(\"%d\\n\", n)` for INT_MIN/INT_MAX.\n\nC. `main.rs` calls `std::process::exit(rc)` after `run_main`. Verify the exit code, and\n   verify stdout is still flushed, and that a seekable stdin is still repositioned.\n   Compare `echo $?` for C vs Rust across many inputs.\n\nD. Thread-safety / reentrancy is NOT a concern (the C is single-threaded) — skip it.\n\nE. Look for any case in indices `data` in -8..=300 where the EXECUTABLES differ in\n   (exit status, stdout bytes) reproducibly over >=20 runs each. Sweep all of them.\n   Do the same for the second stdin line vs the first (the program reads two lines:\n   line 1 feeds goodB2G, line 2 feeds bad).\n\nF. Run a large randomized differential fuzz of the two EXECUTABLES (several thousand\n   cases): random byte strings, random integers, multi-line inputs, over-long lines,\n   whitespace/sign/leading-zero forms, embedded NULs, CRLF, missing trailing newline.\n   Compare (exit status, stdout) exactly. For any mismatch, re-run that exact input\n   20 times on BOTH binaries and only report it if it is REPRODUCIBLE and if the\n   `bad()` index involved is small (< 1000) — otherwise it is the known ASLR band.\n\nG. Check stderr: both should produce nothing on stderr. Verify.\n\nH. Verify `nm -D --defined-only` on both .so files still agree on the 5 exported symbols\n   (printLine, printIntLine, bad, good, main) and that goodG2B/goodB2G are absent.\n\nYou may write scratch files under $TMPDIR (never inside c_src/). Use timeouts on all\ncommands; no single command should run longer than 300 seconds.\n\nReport: a numbered list of CONCRETE, REPRODUCIBLE divergences with (a) exact input,\n(b) C result, (c) Rust result, (d) responsible line in imp.rs/lib.rs/main.rs, and how\nmany of N runs reproduced it. If an area has no divergence, say so explicitly per area.\nBe evidence-based; do not speculate without testing.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-n48Iqv/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-n48Iqv-translated-rust/6de6788a-c8a8-4554-8fe2-4313825db3b2/tasks/aabd720736f391999.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
